  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Monday...\n\nIsolated to scattered showers and a weak thunderstorm or two will\ncontinue eastward early this morning. Additional convection is\nshown by the latest HiRes developing through sunrise and pushing\neastward. A few storms will be capable of producing gusts up to 50\nmph and brief heavy rainfall through this afternoon and evening.\n\nWildfire smoke continues across the region, bringing reductions to\nvisibility and air quality for portions of southern Montana and\nnorthern Wyoming. The smoke has had an effect on daily highs with\ntemperatures being a few degrees cooler than models. Because of \nthis, Heat Products for tomorrow have been cancelled as the high \ntemperatures are not resulting in Major or Extreme HeatRisk.\n\nLook for daily afternoon/evening shower and thunderstorm chances\nthrough the end of the week. There is a better signal for strong \nto severe thunderstorms over southeastern MT along the Dakotas \nborder for Wednesday. The primary concerns will be strong to \nsevere wind gusts up to 65 mph.\n\nMatos",
